
Hospital Management System
==========================

A Ruby on Rails application for managing patients, doctors, appointments,
departments, rooms, beds, and medical records.

Requirements
------------

- Ruby 3.3.11 (see `.ruby-version`)
- Bundler
- SQLite

Getting started
---------------

From the repository root:

```sh
bundle install
bin/rails db:prepare
bin/rails server
```

Open http://localhost:3000. The login page is available at
http://localhost:3000/users/login. To create a patient, use the registration
link on the login page.

The seed task creates an admin account with username `shaheen@gmail.com` and
password `abc123`. Change this password before using a deployed or shared
instance.

Tests
-----

Run the complete test suite with:

```sh
bin/rails test
```

The suite covers startup/health, login and logout, patient registration, and
model validation. Passing automated tests is not a substitute for validating
every workflow in a production-like environment.
